<Project>

  <!--
    Shared build settings for everything under Source\.

    Kept deliberately minimal: this file is evaluated by every project in the tree, so
    each entry here must be a strict improvement with no behavioural change on Windows.

    Reference assemblies for .NET Framework. Since the 2026-10 retarget no SDK-style project
    builds net48 anymore, so this now serves only the old-style projects (Tools\,
    Incubator\, some Backend\Database\ providers) that still carry TargetFrameworkVersion
    v4.8 and are built by no CI gate. On Windows the block is skipped entirely, so desktop
    builds are byte-for-byte unchanged.

    The identical file at ..\Directory.Build.props covers the projects outside Source\
    (Incubator, Tests, Tools). MSBuild stops walking upwards at the first such file it
    finds, so the two must be kept in sync by hand.

    History: this was not enough on its own for years, because MediaPortal.Utilities carried
    non-string .resx resources which abort `dotnet build` with MSB3822/MSB3823 on any host
    without Visual Studio. Those resources were dead and have been deleted, so `dotnet build`
    now handles the whole server solution - see "Which build host, and why it matters" and
    "Compiling on Linux" in scripts/ci/README.md.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(OS)' != 'Windows_NT' AND '$(TargetFramework)' == '' AND '$(TargetFrameworkVersion)' == 'v4.8'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies" Version="1.0.3" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
